===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The short term state of the [[atmosphere]] at a [[specific]] [[time]] and [[place]], including the [[temperature]], [[relative humidity]], [[cloud cover]], [[precipitation]], [[wind]], etc.
#: {{ux|en|What's the '''weather''' like today?}}
#: {{ux|en|We'll go for a walk when the '''weather''''s better.}}
#: {{ux|en|The garden party was called off due to bad '''weather'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Here and there, the '''weather''' on the sea allowed two of their friends to hear and see, too.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1981|author=w:William Irwin Thompson|title=The Time Falling Bodies Take to Light: Mythology, Sexuality and the Origins of Culture|publisher=Rider/Hutchinson & Co.|location=London|page=118|passage=Human beings love to talk about the '''weather'''.}}
# [[unpleasant|Unpleasant]] or [[destructive]] [[atmospheric]] [[condition]]s, and their [[effect]]s.
#: {{ux|en|Wooden garden furniture must be well oiled as it is continuously exposed to '''weather'''.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The direction from which the [[wind]] is blowing; {{non-gloss definition|used attributively to indicate the [[windward]] side}}.
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|3|text=One complained of a bad cold in his head, upon which Jonah mixed him a pitch-like potion of gin and molasses, which he swore was a sovereign cure for all colds and catarrhs whatsoever, never mind of how long standing, or whether caught off the coast of Labrador, or on the '''weather''' side of an ice-island.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|figuratively}} A [[situation]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[storm]]; a [[tempest]].
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aeneis|passage=What gusts of '''weather''' from that gathering cloud / My thoughts presage!}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A light shower of rain.
#: {{rfquotek|en|Wyclif}}

